A growable collection can gain and lose items.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    names ~{String} = {}

    ~names.push("Priya")
]

The binding is mutable because the collection changes.

`push` on a growable collection cannot fail, so it needs no `!` or `catch`. A
fixed-size collection is the one that can be full.

An immutable collection can still be read:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    names = {"Priya", "Rob"}

    first = names.get(0) catch:
        then "guest"
    ;
]
